# gita_anvaya_ch03.itx — anvaya (prose word order) of Bhagavad Gita 3, verses 3.1–3.43
# section: the whole chapter.
#
# PROVENANCE. Transcribed from the anonymous "gItA sandhivigraha anvaya" edition
# on sanskritdocuments.org —
#
#   https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_giitaa/gitAanvayasandhivigraha.itx
#   transliterated and proofread by Sunder Hattangadi, latest update 2008-07-04
#
# That file presents the whole Gita with padaccheda and a traditional anvaya for
# every verse. It is the source of record for the WORDING of every anvaya here:
# nothing below is composed by this project. What this project decides for
# itself is only (a) where one reference sentence that spans two printed verses
# is divided between our verses, and (b) punctuation. Both are marked inline with
# "SPLIT:" and recorded in PROJECT.md. The applier (source/anvaya.py) turns this
# into Devanagari + IAST and writes it into source/ch1.json as each verse's "anv".
#
# FORMAT. ".. S.." is the verse id the anvaya is filed under IN THIS EDITION.
# TRANSCRIBED VERSES: 3.01–3.43, all forty-three.
# The bracketed "ref 2-N" is the verse as the reference prints it, so the mapping
# to the source stays auditable. ITRANS escapes used by the reference:
#   ##!## "!"   ##?## "?"   ##[## "["   ##]## "]"   ##(## "("   ##)## ")"
#   ##'## "'"   .h / H visarga   M anusvara   ~N ङ   ~n ञ   j~n / GY ज्ञ
#   R^i ऋ   Sh ष   A hyphen inside a word marks a compound break and is kept.
# ज्ञ is written j~n throughout here; the reference mixes j~n and GY for the same
# syllable and the applier should not have to know both.
#


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.. 3.01..   {ref 3-1}
he janArdana##!## karmaNaH buddhiH jyAyasI te matA chet.h\, tat.h he keshava##!## mAm.h ghore karmaNi kim.h niyojayasi ##?##

.. 3.02..   {ref 3-2}
vyAmishreNa iva vAkyena me buddhiM mohayasi iva . tat.h nishchitya ekaM vada\, yena aham.h shreyaH ApnuyAm.h .

.. 3.03..   {ref 3-3}
he anagha##!## asmin.h loke sA~NkhyAnAm.h GYAna-yogena\, yoginAm.h karma-yogena dvividhA niShThA purA mayA proktA .

.. 3.04..   {ref 3-4}
karmaNAm.h anArambhAt.h puruShaH naiShkarmyaM na ashnute . ##(##karmaNAM##)## cha sa.nnyasanAt.h eva siddhim.h na samadhigachChati .

.. 3.05..   {ref 3-5}
kashchit.h jAtu kShaNam.h api akarmakR^it.h na hi tiShThati . prakR^itijaiH guNaiH sarvaH hi avashaH karma kAryate .

.. 3.06..   {ref 3-6}
yaH karma-indriyANi sa.nyamya\, manasA indriyArthAn.h smaran.h Aste\, saH vimUDhAtmA mithyAchAraH uchyate .

.. 3.07..   {ref 3-7}
he arjuna ##!## yaH tu manasA indriyANi niyamya\, asaktaH karma-indriyaiH karma-yogam.h Arabhate\, saH vishiShyate .

.. 3.08..   {ref 3-8}
tvaM niyatam.h karma kuru\, akarmaNaH hi karma jyAyaH . te sharIra-yAtrA cha api akarmaNaH na prasid.hdhyet.h .

.. 3.09..   {ref 3-9}
yaGYArthAt.h karmaNaH anyatra ayam.h lokaH karma-bandhanaH . he kaunteya##!## mukta-sa~NgaH tat.h artham.h karma samAchara .

.. 3.10..   {ref 3-10}
purA prajApatiH saha-yaGYAH prajAH sR^iShTvA ##'##anena ##(##yUyaM##)## prasaviShyadhvam.h\, eShaH vaH iShTa-kAmadhuk.h astu##'## ##(##iti##)##  uvAcha .

.. 3.11..   {ref 3-11}
anena ##(##yUyaM##)## devAn.h bhAvayata\, te devAH vaH bhAvayantu\, ##(##evaM##)## parasparaM bhAvayantaH param.h shreyaH avApsyatha .

.. 3.12..   {ref 3-12}
yaGYa-bhAvitAH devAH vaH iShTAn.h bhogAn.h dAsyante . taiH dattAn.h ebhyaH apradAya\, yaH bhu~Nkte\, saH hi stenaH eva .

.. 3.13..   {ref 3-13}
yaGYa-shiShTa AshinaH santaH sarva-kilbiShaiH muchyante . ye tu Atma-kAraNAt.h pachanti\, te pApAH aghaM bhu~njate .

.. 3.14..   {ref 3-14}
bhUtAni annAt.h bhavanti\, parjanyAt.h anna-sambhavaH\, parjanyaH yaGYAt.h bhavati\, yaGYaH karma-samudbhavaH .

.. 3.15..   {ref 3-15}
karma brahma-udbhava.n viddhi\, brahma akShara-samudbhavam.h\, tasmAt.h sarvagataM brahma yaGYe nityaM pratiShThitam.h .

.. 3.16..   {ref 3-16}
he pArtha##!## evaM pravartitam.h chakram.h yaH iha na anuvartayati\, saH indriya-ArAmaH aghAyuH mogham.h jIvati .

.. 3.17..   {ref 3-17}
yaH tu mAnavaH Atma-ratiH eva\, Atma-tR^iptaH cha\, Atmani eva cha santuShTaH syAt.h tasya kAryam.h na vidyate .

.. 3.18..   {ref 3-18}
iha tasya kR^itena arthaH na eva\, na akR^itena kashchana\, na cha asya sarva-bhUteShu kashchit.h artha-vyapAshrayaH .

.. 3.19..   {ref 3-19}
tasmAt.h ##(##tvaM##)## asaktaH ##(##san.h##)## satatam.h kAryam.h karma samAchara\, hi pUruShaH asaktaH ##(##san.h##)## karma Acharan.h\, param.h Apnoti .

.. 3.20..   {ref 3-20}
hi janaka-AdayaH karmaNA eva sa.nsiddhim.h AsthitAH . ##(##tvaM##)## api loka-sa.ngraham.h eva sampashyan.h kartum.h arhasi .

.. 3.21..   {ref 3-21}
yat.h yat.h shreShThaH Acharati tat.h tat.h eva itaraH janaH ##(## Acharati##)##. saH yat.h pramANam.h kurute\, lokaH tat.h anuvartate .

.. 3.22..   {ref 3-22}
he pArtha##!## ##(##yadyapi##)## me triShu lokeShu ki~nchana kartavyam.h na asti\, anavAptam.h avAptavyam.h cha na ##(##asti, tathA api ahaM##)## karmaNi varte eva .

.. 3.23..   {ref 3-23}
yadi hi ahaM atandritaH ##(##san.h##)## karmaNi jAtu na varteyam.h\, ##(##tarhi##)## he pArtha##!## manuShyAH sarvashaH mama vartma anuvartante .

.. 3.24..   {ref 3-24}
aham.h karma na kuryAm.h chet.h ime lokAH utsIdeyuH\, sa~Nkarasya kartA syAm.h imAH prajAH cha upahanyAm.h .

.. 3.25..   {ref 3-25}
he bhArata##!## avidvA.nsaH yathA karmaNi saktAH ##(##karma##)## kurvanti\, tathA loka-sa.ngraham.h chikIrShuH vidvAn.h asaktaH ##(##san.h karma##)## kuryAt.h .

.. 3.26..   {ref 3-26}
vidvAn.h karma-sa~NginAm.h aGYAnAm.h buddhi-bhedam.h na janayet.h ##(##kintu##)## yuktaH samAcharan.h sarva-karmANi joShayet.h .

.. 3.27..   {ref 3-27}
prakR^iteH guNaiH karmANi sarvashaH kriyamANAni ##(##santi, parantu##)## aha~NkAra-vimUDha-AtmA ##'##aham.h##'## kartA iti manyate .

.. 3.28..   {ref 3-28}
he mahAbAho##!## guNa-karma-vibhAgayoH tattvavit.h tu ##'##guNAH guNeShu vartante##'## iti matvA na sajjate .

.. 3.29..   {ref 3-29}
prakR^iteH guNa-sammUDhAH guNa-karmasu sajjante\, tAn.h akR^itsnavidaH mandAn.h kR^itsnavit.h na vichAlayet.h .

.. 3.30..   {ref 3-30}
mayi adhyAtma-chetasA sarvANi karmANi sa.nnyasya nirAshIH nirmamaH vigata-jvaraH bhUtvA\, yudhyasva .

.. 3.31..   {ref 3-31}
ye mAnavAH shraddhAvantaH anasUyantaH idam.h me matam.h nityam.h anutiShThanti\, te api karmabhiH muchyante .

.. 3.32..   {ref 3-32}
ye tu etat.h abhyasUyantaH me matam.h na anutiShThanti\, tAn.h sarva-GYAna-vimUDhAn.h achetasaH naShTAn.h viddhi .

.. 3.33..   {ref 3-33}
GYAnavAn.h api svasyAH prakR^iteH sadR^isham.h cheShTate . bhUtAni prakR^itim.h yAnti . nigrahaH kim.h kariShyati ##?##

.. 3.34..   {ref 3-34}
indriyasya-arthe indriyasya rAga-dveShau vyavasthitau\, tayoH vasham na AgachChet.h . tau hi asya paripanthinau .

.. 3.35..   {ref 3-35}
svanuShThitAt.h paradharmAt.h viguNaH svadharmaH ##(##api##)## shreyAn.h . svadharme nidhanam.h shreyaH . paradharmaH bhaya-AvahaH .

.. 3.36..   {ref 3-36}
he vArShNeya##!## atha kena prayuktaH ayaM pUruShaH anichChan.h api\, balAt.h niyojitaH iva pApam.h charati##?##

.. 3.37..   {ref 3-37}
rajaH guNa-samudbhavaH mahA-pApmA mahA-ashanaH eShaH kAmaH\, eShaH krodhaH ##(##asti; tvaM##)## enam.h iha vairiNam.h viddhi .

.. 3.38..   {ref 3-38}
yathA dhUmena vahniH\, yathA cha malena AdarshaH\, Avriyate\, ##(##yathA##)## ulbena garbhaH AvR^itaH\, tathA tena idam.h AvR^itam.h .

.. 3.39..   {ref 3-39}
he kaunteya##!## nityavairiNA etena duShpUreNa kAmarUpeNa cha analena GYAninaH GYAnam.h AvR^itam.h .

.. 3.40..   {ref 3-40}
indriyANi manaH buddhiH asya adhiShThAnam.h uchyate . eShaH etaiH GYAnam.h AvR^itya dehinam.h vimohayati .

.. 3.41..   {ref 3-41}
he bharatarShabha##!## tasmAt.h tvam.h Adau indriyANi niyamya\, GYAna-viGYAna-nAshanam.h enaM pApmAnam.h prajahi hi .

.. 3.42..   {ref 3-42}
indriyANi parANi AhuH\, indriyebhyaH manaH param.h\, manasaH tu buddhiH parA\, yaH tu buddheH parataH saH ##(##AtmA asti##)##.

.. 3.43..   {ref 3-43}
he mahAbAho##!## evam.h ##(##AtmAnaM##)## buddheH param.h buddhvA AtmanA AtmAnam.h sa.nstabhya\, kAma-rUpam.h durAsadam.h shatrum.h jahi .
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE THIS EDITION DIFFERS FROM THE REFERENCE
#
# 3.18. The reference (anvayasandhivigraha) writes this verse's ellipsis out in
#   full, supplying api and tathā, repeating asya, and repeating arthaḥ. That is
#   a commentarial expansion, not the verse: its sentence carries words and a
#   meaning that ours does not.
#
#   Gita Press's Padachchheda-Anvaya (book code 17) supplies nothing here. Its
#   padachheda for this verse is our verse word for word — na, eva, tasya,
#   kṛtena, arthaḥ, na, akṛtena, iha, kaścana, na, ca, asya, sarvabhūteṣu,
#   kaścit, arthavyapāśrayaḥ — and its anvaya keeps that order without adding
#   to it. So the anvaya above is Gita Press's, and the reference's expansion is
#   recorded here instead of being used. The supplied api is an Advaita gloss on
#   akṛtena ("even by non-action") — the kind of thing a paraphrase may say and
#   a construal, which claims to hold only the verse's words, must not.
#
#   This is the one verse in chapters 1–3 where the two witnesses disagree about
#   what the sentence IS, rather than about how to spell a word of it.
